  "description": "New Jersey's 5th Congressional District covers parts of Bergen, Passaic, and Sussex counties in the northern part of the state, stretching from the New York City suburbs of Bergen County to rural areas in Sussex County. Incumbent Democrat Josh Gottheimer, first elected in 2016, is seeking a sixth term against Republican nominee Sean Kirrane and independent candidate Adam Rueda. The district has a voter registration advantage for Democrats (35% Democratic, 26% Republican, rest unaffiliated), and Cook Political Report rates the race as Solid Democratic. Gottheimer has positioned himself as a moderate, fiscally disciplined Democrat and co-chair of the bipartisan Problem Solvers Caucus, while Kirrane is a business executive running as a socially moderate, fiscally disciplined Republican focused on affordability and government reform.",
